.TH OBM 1 "September 2026" "omarchy-batch-monitor 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
obm \- OpenAI Batch API status monitor for Omarchy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B obm
[\fB--api-key\fR \fIKEY\fR]
[\fB--refresh\fR \fISECS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B obm
is a terminal UI that lists and auto-refreshes OpenAI Batch API jobs, with a
detail panel and the ability to cancel a running batch.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --api-key " " \fIKEY\fR
OpenAI API key. Defaults to the \fBOPENAI_API_KEY\fR environment variable,
then \fBapi_key\fR in the config file.
.TP
.BR --refresh " " \fISECS\fR
Seconds between automatic refreshes. Default 15.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Optional config file at \fI~/.config/omarchy-batch-monitor/config.toml\fR:
.RS
.nf
api_key = "sk-..."
organization = "org-..."
project = "proj_..."
refresh_secs = 15
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fBOPENAI_ORG_ID\fR, \fBOPENAI_PROJECT_ID\fR, and \fBOPENAI_API_BASE\fR are
also honored.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B j/k, arrows
select next/previous batch
.TP
.B g/G, Home/End
select first/last
.TP
.B r
refresh now
.TP
.B c
cancel the selected batch (with confirmation)
.TP
.B s
toggle sort order
.TP
.B ?
toggle help
.TP
.B q, Esc
quit
.SH SEE ALSO
OpenAI Batch API guide: https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/batch
